course: dictionary
lesson: 317
title: Science words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out the meaning of a new word from the words around it. These are its context. «An anemometer measures how fast the wind blows.» The word measures tells you the anemometer is used for measuring, and the wind blows tells you what it measures.
explain: So an anemometer must be a tool, something you use to find out a number. Ask yourself: what would fit here instead of the hard word? A tool that measures wind speed fits, so that is probably right. Then check it by putting your meaning into the sentence.
explain: Science words often have a simple meaning that you can test. Pupils make a simple anemometer from paper cups and straws. The cups spin in the wind, and the faster they spin, the faster the wind is blowing. The spinning is the clue that shows what the tool is for.
fact: An anemometer is an instrument that measures how fast the wind is blowing.
fact: Wind speed can be measured in kilometres per hour, miles per hour or knots.
fact: In science lessons, pupils can make a simple anemometer from paper cups and straws.
fact: The faster the cups spin in the wind, the faster the wind is blowing.
fact: Weather stations use anemometers to keep track of the wind.
exercise: «An anemometer measures how fast the wind blows.» What does an anemometer do? | Tells the time | *Measures how fast the wind is blowing | Measures how much rain falls | Makes the wind blow faster
exercise: In a science lesson, pupils can make a simple anemometer from which materials? | *Paper cups and straws | Wooden blocks and string | Glass bottles and tape | Sand and bricks
exercise: Which unit can be used to measure wind speed? | Litres | *Kilometres per hour | Metres squared | Kilograms
test: Why do the cups on a simple anemometer spin faster? | *Because the wind is blowing faster | Because it is raining harder | Because the cups are heavier | Because the straws are longer
test: Which word in «An anemometer measures how fast the wind blows.» is the name of the tool? | wind | *anemometer | blows | fast
exam: What is an anemometer? | A type of weather cloud | A kind of cup that holds water | A tool that measures how much rain falls | *A tool that measures how fast the wind is blowing
